  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban Council, polled Wednesday 17 May 1961 (Belfast News-Letter, 18 May 1961, p. 10; Londonderry Sentinel, 24 May 1961, p. 11). Eleven candidates for nine seats; all members of the old council were returned. Total poll 1,376 (76.6 per cent). The two defeated candidates, William Morrison and Alexander Semple, both new, are named in the Londonderry Sentinel.",
